mike/bus/inbox/quant-skeptic.jsonl:146:{"event_id": "e8767367-c6b5-487f-876e-25c1da89f469", "ts": "[REDACTED]0:53:56Z", "agent_id": "quant-skeptic", "event_type": "verification", "topic": "VERIFY: tv1-execution-p1p2p5-implementation-20260812", "payload": {"finding_topic": "tv1-execution-p1p2p5-implementation-20260812", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "pass — no BQ forward columns anywhere (minute-bar execution sim, not signal research). exp_ceiling_tolerance.py uses adv20=rolling(20).mean().shift(1) and anchor=dd.iloc[pos-lag]['close'] (lag>=5), both causal. P2's f(t) is a historical median profile applied by wall-clock minute. CAVEAT (not leakage, but adjacent): mike/[REDACTED]retionary_accumulation_inject.py:145-157 sets to_ts=now_ict() and takes closes[-n:] with NO timestamp filter, so if DNSE /ohlc 1D returns today's in-progress bar the anchor includes today's live price despite the docstring promising 'phien DA HOAN TAT'. Path has never run live; the 49-case selfcheck injects anchor_prices by hand and cannot catch it.", "oos_robustness": "fail (non-fatal) — no IS/OOS split at all. tau=3%, c=0.50 and the 18-point expected_volume_curve are all selected on the same 23-ticker x ~80-session sample (2026-04-20 onward). f(t) is fit via build_profile() on the last 120 sessions, which overlap the 80 sessions used to evaluate P2 — in-sample curve fitting. Mitigated but not eliminated: f(t) is a low-DoF median object and is double-guarded (max with real volume, plus clamp on real tape). Payload honestly flags 'P2 CHUA TUNG chay tren tape that' and gates on a >=4-week paper trial.", "panel_curation_bias": "fail (non-fatal) — cohort is 100 hand-screened thin tickers (ADV20 0.15-2.5bn) in data/thin_cohort_bq.csv; I verified TV1 and DGC, the actual live targets, are NOT in it (grep -c '^(TV1|DGC),' = 0). Payload flags this for f(t) only; it applies equally to tau=3% and to the fill model. No >30%-CAGR-style claim is made, so the classic mirage does not apply — this is an execution-mechanics study, and the bias direction is unknown rather than favorable.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — I re-ran all three selfchecks myself: 49/0, 39/0, 44/0 PASS/FAIL with rc=0, exactly matching 49/39/44. AST diff of _child_qty confirms the flag-OFF path is expression-identical to HEAD; _limit_price byte-IDENTICAL (S24 intact); DEFAULTS['expected_volume_pacing_enabled'] is False. I independently ran the S23 control experiment (git checkout -- the 4 files, re-run the 4 reds): FAIL lines byte-identical to the working tree in all 4, confirming pre-existing. Files restored and cmp-verified.", "param_overfit": "pass (with reservation) — tau shows a monotone plateau, not a magic point: fill 0.627/0.708/0.750/0.783/0.797 across tau=0/1/2/3/5% and the sign holds across lag 5/10/20; kappa robustness holds across 0.15/0.34/0.60 with no sign change (all reproduced exactly). RESERVATION: the tail clamp c=0.50 is a single hardcoded value with zero sensitivity analysis, and it is the one parameter carrying the tail-risk guarantee.", "capacity_adv_realism": "pass — capacity IS the subject, not a hidden assumption; the study deliberately targets thin names. Payload states the honest gap unprompted: simulation caps orders at 20% ADV/session while real confirmed fills reach only ~3.86% ADV/session, cross-referenced to the open warning in kb/projects/lag-adv-filter-tracking.md, and gates deployment on a >=4-week paper trial.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "fail (does not void headline) — IMPLEMENTATION.md:92 declares the clamp form cV-F 'SAI', but that is precisely the formula in exp_expected_floor.py (headroom = int(TAIL_CLAMP*(cum_vol+avail)) - [REDACTED]) that generated EVERY P2 number in the report. The two encode opposite impact models (impl: our fill adds to V; sim: our fill displaces other buyers) and each is correct in its own world; the disagreement was never surfaced. I re-ran the sim under the deployed formula AND placement (clamp on allowance at slice time, not on realized fill): fill 0.829 vs the reported 0.860. Shipped P2 gain over current (0.783) is +4.6pp, not the implied +7.7pp. Safety survives (mean tape 13.3% vs 14.6%, p95 29.9% vs 34.0%, >50% tape 0.0% under both). Selfcheck E1 asserts the <=50% invariant with 'V += qty' — the same additivity premise the formula was derived from, so it is circular w.r.t. this issue. Separately verified E5 arithmetic is internally consistent (f(870)=0.958, adv_shares=35226, floor=3522, ceil=10124, clamp=1000).", "look_ahead_leak_note": "see look_ahead_leak"}, "independent_recompute": "Reproduced exactly from the cited CSVs: N=1840, enough=1538, S0=0.804, S2=0.910, +10.6pp; kappa table 0.547/0.615, 0.681/0.776, 0.727/0.841; L1 6.3%/16.4%; the full P1 tau x lag table (fill and price/anchor to the quoted digit; '%phien fill=0' is literally `[REDACTED] < LOT`, e.g. 22.4%/6.1% vs 20.8%/5.1% for `[REDACTED] == 0`); 6.9%/3.5%/12.7% via a live re-run of exp_participation_bound.py; config expected_volume_curve matches out/cum_volume_profile.csv at all 18 points; P2 table 0.860/4.3%/14.6%/34.0%/0.0% reproduced exactly under the research clamp. Re-ran all 3 new selfchecks (49/39/44, rc=0) and ran the S23 control experiment myself (4 reds identical on clean HEAD). NON-MATCH: re-running the P2 sim under the DEPLOYED clamp formula and placement yields fill 0.829, not the reported 0.860.", "killer_objection": "No number in the report describes the code that will actually ship. IMPLEMENTATION.md calls the research's own clamp formula (cV-F) 'wrong' and substitutes (cV-F)/(1-c) applied at slice time on the allowance rather than at fill time on the realized fill — a different mechanism, never re-simulated. My re-run puts shipped P2 at fill 0.829, so its gain over current is +4.6pp rather than the +7.7pp the report's 0.860 implies (~40% overstatement of the increment). Direction and safety survive, but the paper trial must be sized against 0.829, and selfcheck E1 cannot arbitrate because it assumes the same additive-tape model the deployed formula was derived from.", "recommended_reruns": ["Re-run exp_expected_floor.py with the DEPLOYED clamp (allowance-level, (c*V-F)/(1-c)) and republish the P2 row; my probe gives fill 0.829 / mean tape 13.3% / p95 29.9% / >50% tape 0.0% (N=1840, kappa=0.34, tau=3%, lag=5).", "Add a sim mode where our fill does NOT add to the tape (displacement world) and confirm the <=50% invariant still holds under the deployed formula — E1's 'V += qty' assumes the favorable model and cannot test this.", "Fix anchor_prices_for(): read the DNSE 't' array and drop any bar dated today (or set to_ts to yesterday's close) so the docstring's 'phien DA HOAN TAT' is enforced in code; add a selfcheck case that feeds a raw DNSE-shaped payload containing a same-day bar.", "Before the first paper enable of P1, exercise anchor_prices_for() against the live API in dry-run and confirm the [FAILSAFE] branches print — the payload's own precondition, still outstanding.", "Add a c sensitivity sweep (0.35/0.50/0.65) — c=0.50 is the sole parameter carrying the tail guarantee and currently has none.", "Recompute tau and f(t) on TV1/DGC's own bars (both absent from the 100-name cohort) before treating tau=3% as calibrated for the live targets.", "Separate pass on the 4 selfchecks red since [REDACTED] (do not bundle), and add a failing-selfcheck sweep to weekly_ops_audit.sh as the payload proposes — 2 days of silent red is the more alarming finding."], "summary": "The headline is a scope-and-safety claim and it holds under every check I could run. I independently re-ran all three new selfchecks (49/39/44, rc=0, zero FAIL), confirmed via AST diff that the flag-OFF path in _child_qty is expression-identical to HEAD and that _limit_price is untouched (S24 intact), and reproduced the S23 control experiment myself — reverting the 4 production files to clean HEAD yields byte-identical FAIL lines in all 4 red selfchecks, so they are genuinely pre-existing HYBRID-fill-timing fallout and not P1/P2/P5 regressions. Every research number I could recompute from the cited CSVs matched exactly, including 1538/0.804/0.910/+10.6pp, the full P1 tau x lag table, 6.9%/3.5%/12.7%, and the 18-point f(t) curve against cum_volume_profile.csv. Two defects matter before anything is enabled, neither voiding the headline: (1) the deployed tail clamp is not the one the research measured — IMPLEMENTATION.md declares the research's own cV-F formula 'wrong' and ships (cV-F)/(1-c) at a different point in the loop, and my re-run of the sim under the shipped mechanism gives fill 0.829 rather than the reported 0.860, cutting P2's claimed gain from +7.7pp to +4.6pp (safety is unaffected and in fact slightly better); (2) anchor_prices_for() has no same-day-bar exclusion despite a docstring promising completed sessions only, on a path that has never run against the live API and that the 49-case selfcheck cannot reach because it injects anchors by hand. Secondary: no OOS split, c=0.50 has no sensitivity, and TV1/DGC are absent from the 100-name cohort the parameters were tuned on. P5 is safe to enable now; P2 should be paper-traded against a corrected 0.829 baseline; P1 should not be enabled until the anchor same-day filter is fixed and the live DNSE path is exercised in dry-run."}, "kb_version": 2081, "trace_id": "Taylor_20260812_095213"}
